    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Of course! A typical 3-step progressive discipline process consists of verbal warning, written warning, and final written warning before proceeding to termination. Verbal warnings address the misconduct, written warnings document the behavior and desired improvements, and final written warnings give the final opportunity to correct course before termination is confirmed. Each step confirms ongoing communication with the employee and provides a clear path for improvement or potential dismissal. It’s essential to document all instances and feedback during the process to ensure fair handling.",
