      "content": "When considering moving from a verbal to a written warning, vital red flags include repeated instances of misconduct, failure to correct issues after verbal warning, possible risks to the team or organization, or when fairness and thoroughness necessitate documentation. Issues that escalate in severity or frequency, such as unprofessional behavior or safety violations, should also prompt a written warning to ensure accountability and a clear record. Uniform application of discipline policies across the organization is also important to maintain fairness and trust among team members.",
