      "content": "That's a valid concern. Subtly undermining colleagues or the team may not come with obvious signs like loud or aggressive behavior. You can catch these kinds of issues by maintaining open lines of communication, seeking insight from multiple sources, and paying close attention to inconsistencies in behavior or performance. Subtle signs of undermining may include passive aggressiveness, small-scale fostering of conflict, or feigning compliance while actually disregarding guidelines. Documentation of these occurrences and regular check-ins with team members can help you create an accurate picture of the situation. Additionally, fostering a team culture where peers feel comfortable speaking up can help identify less obvious issues early on. It is important to approach these situations with sensitivity to avoid false accusations and to preserve trust within the team.",
